    ],
    "venue": "IEEE VIS: Visualization and Visual Analytics",
    "year": 2023,
    "description": "We developed ManimML, an open-source Python library for easily generating animations of ML algorithms directly from code. ManimML has a familiar syntax for specifying neural networks that mimics popular deep learning frameworks like Pytorch. A user can take a preexisting neural network architecture and easily write a specification for an animation in ManimML, which will then automatically compose animations for different components of the system into a final animation of the entire neural network.",
