    "venue": "arXiv preprint",
    "year": 2025,
    "description": "What exactly makes a particular image unsafe? We introduce SafetyPairs, a scalable framework for generating counterfactual pairs of images that differ only in the features relevant to a given safety policy. Using image editing models, we make targeted changes to images that alter their safety labels while leaving safety-irrelevant details unchanged. We release a benchmark containing over 3,020 SafetyPair images spanning 9 safety categories, providing the first systematic resource for studying fine-grained image safety distinctions.",
